Package: BayCAST
Type: Package
Title: BayCAST: Bayesian Current-status AFT with Subgroup-Targeted Inference
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Jihyun",
           family = "Kim",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "kim02688@umn.edu")
Description: Implements a Bayesian semiparametric accelerated failure-time model
    with a Dirichlet-process mixture over a latent factor structure. Posterior
    inference is performed by Gibbs sampling using the Kalli-Griffin-Walker
    slice sampler for the DP stick-breaking representation, with stochastic
    search variable selection (point-mass spike-and-slab) on the factor loadings.
    The model is designed for survival data with high-dimensional omics
    covariates and is described in <preprint URL TBD>.
